git show <commit-id> --stat
git show <commit-id>

5. Compare one file across commits

bash
git log --oneline -- <path/to/file>                 # history of that file
git diff <older-commit> <newer-commit> -- <path/to/file>
git diff origin/master <your-branch> -- <path/to/file>   # master version vs yours

For example, with the Datavant file:

bash
git diff origin/master...<your-branch> -- snowpark/datavant-mra-etl/src/main/scala/com/anthem/hca/intervention/datavantmbr/DatavantMbrProvETL.scala

6. Side-by-side view (easier to show on screen)

bash
git difftool origin/master...<your-branch> -- <path/to/file>
